- **cloud_ssd**: standard SSD.
- **cloud_essd**: ESSD.
- **cloud_auto** (default): premium performance disk.', example='cloud_auto', position='Query'),
  diskName?: string(name='DiskName', description='The name of the cloud disk. The name must be 2 to 128 characters in length and can contain letters and digits in the Unicode Letter category. It can also contain colons (:), underscores (_), periods (.), and hyphens (-).', example='testDisk', position='Query'),
  instanceChargeType?: string(name='InstanceChargeType', description='The billing method. Valid values:

- **Postpaid**: pay-as-you-go. Cloud disks of this billing method do not need to be mounted to instances. You can also mount a pay-as-you-go cloud disk to an instance of any billing method when you create it as needed.
- **Prepaid**: subscription. Cloud disks of this billing method must be mounted to subscription instances. You must specify the **InstanceId** parameter, which is the instance ID of a subscription instance.', example='Postpaid', position='Query'),
  instanceId?: string(name='InstanceId', description='Instance ID of the instance to which the cloud disk is attached. If **InstanceChargeType** is set to **Prepaid**, you must specify instance ID of a subscription instance.', example='rc-v28c6k3jupp61m2t****', position='Query'),
  performanceLevel?: string(name='PerformanceLevel', description='The performance level of the ESSD cloud disk. Valid values:

- **PL0**: A single ESSD can deliver up to 10,000 random read/write IOPS.
- **PL1** (default): A single ESSD can deliver up to 50,000 random read/write IOPS.
- **PL2**: A single ESSD can deliver up to 100,000 random read/write IOPS.
- **PL3**: A single ESSD can deliver up to 1,000,000 random read/write IOPS.

For more information about how to select the performance level of an ESSD, see [ESSDs](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2859916.html).', example='PL1', position='Query'),
  period?: int32(name='Period', description='A reserved parameter. You do not need to specify this parameter.', example='none', position='Query'),
  periodUnit?: string(name='PeriodUnit', description='A reserved parameter. You do not need to specify this parameter.', example='none', position='Query'),
  regionId: string(name='RegionId', description='The region ID. You can call the DescribeRegions operation to query region IDs.

This parameter is required.', example='cn-hangzhou', position='Query'),
  resourceGroupId?: string(name='ResourceGroupId', description='The ID of the resource group.', example='rg-ac****', position='Query'),
  size?: int32(name='Size', description='The size of the cloud disk. Unit: GiB. You must specify this parameter. Valid values:

- **cloud_efficiency**: 20 to 32,768.
- **cloud_ssd**: 20 to 32,768.
- **cloud_auto**: 1 to 65,536.
- **cloud_essd**: The valid values vary based on the value of **PerformanceLevel**.
  - PL0: 1 to 65,536.
  - PL1: 20 to 65,536.
  - PL2: 461 to 65,536.
  - PL3: 1,261 to 65,536.

If you specify the **SnapshotId** parameter and the size of the snapshot is greater than the value of **Size**, the created cloud disk is the same size as the snapshot. If the snapshot size is smaller than the value of **Size**, the created cloud disk is the size specified by **Size**.', example='2000', position='Query'),
  snapshotId?: string(name='SnapshotId', description='The ID of the snapshot used to create the cloud disk.

- You can use RDS Custom snapshots and ECS snapshots (excluding shared snapshots).
- If the size of the snapshot specified by **SnapshotId** is greater than the value of **Size**, the created cloud disk is the same size as the snapshot. If the snapshot size is smaller than the value of **Size**, the created cloud disk is the size specified by **Size**.
- You cannot use snapshots to create ephemeral disks.
- Snapshots created on or before July 15, 2013 cannot be used to create cloud disks.', example='rcds-umtnkvevqbu****', position='Query'),
  tag?: [ 
    {
      key?: string(name='Key', description='The tag key. You can create up to N tag keys at a time. Valid values of N: **1** to **20**. The tag key cannot be an empty string.', example='testkey1'),
