>This parameter takes effect only when **UpgradeTime** is set to **SpecifyTime**.', example='2020-01-15T00:00:00Z', position='Query'),
  targetMinorVersion?: string(name='TargetMinorVersion', description='The target minor database version. Format:
* **PostgreSQL**: `rds_postgres_<Major version number>00_<Minor version number>`. Example: `rds_postgres_1200_20200830` for PostgreSQL 12 version 20200830.
* **MySQL**: `<Instance edition>_<Minor version number>`. Examples: `rds_20200229`, `xcluster_20200229`, and `xcluster80_20200229`. The instance editions are as follows:
    * **rds**: high availability series or Basic Edition.
    * **xcluster**: MySQL 5.7 RDS Enterprise Edition.
    * **xcluster80**: MySQL 8.0 RDS Enterprise Edition.
* **SQL Server**: `<Minor version number>`. Example: `15.0.4073.23`.

If you do not specify this parameter, the instance is upgraded to the latest minor database version by default.
> For more information about minor database versions, see [Release notes for minor engine versions of ApsaraDB RDS for PostgreSQL](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/126002.html), [Release notes for minor engine versions of ApsaraDB RDS for MySQL](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/96060.html), and [Release notes for minor engine versions of ApsaraDB RDS for SQL Server](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/213577.html).', example='xcluster80_20210305', position='Query'),
  upgradeTime?: string(name='UpgradeTime', description='The time when the upgrade is performed. Valid values:

